    "input": "search_query: Dear Northwind Outdoor Support Team,\n\nI hope this message finds you well. I am writing to respectfully report an issue regarding my recent purchase of a camping tent. Unfortunately, upon unpacking it, I discovered a significant tear in the waterproof coating. I understand that your policy requires damaged items to be returned within 10 days, and I have already initiated the return process to ensure I am well within that timeframe. However, I am concerned about the refund amount. The tent cost $650.00, but I noticed that full refunds are capped at $500.00 per item. Given that the item was defective upon arrival, I was hoping for a full reimbursement of the purchase price rather than a partial refund. Could you please clarify if there are any exceptions to this cap for manufacturing defects? I have always appreciated your excellent service and would love to resolve this matter amicably. Thank you for your time and assistance.\n\nSincerely,\nArthur",
